{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"The trust’s **board of trustees**, typically acting through its **audit committee**, selects and oversees the independent auditor for the trust and its series. Shareholders generally do **not** have to ratify that selection: ratification is not required by federal securities law or the usual NYSE Arca listing standards for ETFs. It may be omitted when the trust’s governing documents and applicable state law do not require a shareholder vote, and the board/audit committee makes the appointment.\n\nCheck the trust’s declaration, bylaws, audit-committee charter, and exchange listing rules for any trust-specific requirement; voluntary ratification may still be submitted as a governance practice."}}
